- ### `unit`
- Convert between physical units (length, weight, temperature, volume, speed, etc.).
- - `VALUE` (required) — Numeric value to convert
- - `FROM` (required) — Source unit (e.g., km, lb, celsius)
- - `TO` (required) — Target unit (e.g., miles, kg, fahrenheit)
- VALUE=100 FROM=km TO=miles bash scripts/script.sh unit
- ### `currency`
- Convert between currencies using stored exchange rates.
- - `AMOUNT` (required) — Amount to convert
- - `FROM` (required) — Source currency code (e.g., USD)
- - `TO` (required) — Target currency code (e.g., EUR)
- ### `encoding`
- Convert text between encodings (UTF-8, ASCII, Base64, URL encoding, etc.).
- - `INPUT` (required) — Input text or file path
- - `FROM` (required) — Source encoding
- - `TO` (required) — Target encoding
- - `IS_FILE` — Set to `true` if INPUT is a file path (default: false)
- ### `color`
- Convert between color formats (HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV, CMYK).
- - `COLOR` (required) — Color value (e.g., "#FF5733", "rgb(255,87,51)")
- - `TO` — Target format: `hex`, `rgb`, `hsl`, `hsv`, `cmyk` (default: all)
- ### `time`
- Convert between time zones or timestamp formats.
- - `TIME` (required) — Time value (ISO 8601 or Unix timestamp)
- - `FROM` — Source timezone (default: UTC)
- - `TO` — Target timezone (e.g., Asia/Shanghai, US/Eastern)
- ### `number`
- Convert numbers between bases (binary, octal, decimal, hexadecimal).
- - `VALUE` (required) — Number to convert
- - `FROM` — Source base: `bin`, `oct`, `dec`, `hex` (default: dec)
- - `TO` — Target base (default: all)
- ### `batch`
- Run multiple conversions from a batch file.
- - `INPUT` (required) — Path to batch file (JSONL with conversion specs)
- - `OUTPUT` — Output file for results (default: stdout)
- ### `list`
- List supported conversion types and available units/formats.
- - `TYPE` — Specific type to list: `unit`, `currency`, `encoding`, `color`, `time`, `number` (default: all)
- ### `config`
- View or update configuration settings.
- - `KEY` — Configuration key to set
- - `VALUE` — Configuration value
- ### `help`
- Display usage information and available commands.
- ### `version`
- Display the current version of the convert tool.
- ## Data Storage
- Conversion history is stored in `~/.convert/data.jsonl`. Each record contains:
- - `id` — Unique conversion identifier
- - `timestamp` — ISO 8601 time
- - `type` — Conversion type (unit, file, currency, etc.)
- - `input` — Input value/parameters
- - `output` — Conversion result
- - `from_format` — Source format/unit
- - `to_format` — Target format/unit
- ## Configuration
- Config stored in `~/.convert/config.json`:
- - `default_currency_base` — Default base currency (default: USD)
- - `decimal_places` — Decimal precision (default: 6)
- - `save_history` — Whether to save conversion history (default: true)
